---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Credits from '../components/Credits.astro'
import {getSettings} from '../lib/settings'

const s = await getSettings()
// Controller per the artist contract
const company = 'Arketyp Artist Services AB'
const label = 'Skolhaus'
const contactEmail = 'info@arketyp.se'
const updated = '2 November 2026'
---

<Base title="Privacy & Cookies" description={`How ${s.artistName} and ${label} handle your personal data.`}>
  <header class="top">
    <a href="/">{s.artistName}</a>
  </header>

  <main class="policy">
    <h1>Privacy &amp; Cookies</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      This website is run by {company} through its record label {label}, which releases the music of {s.artistName}.
      {company} is the controller of the personal data collected here.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>We only collect what you give us when you sign up for updates:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Email address</li>
      <li>Phone number, if you add it for SMS updates</li>
      <li>Country, so we can tell you about shows and releases where you are</li>
      <li>When and where you signed up, and that you agreed to receive updates</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you accept cookies, we also collect statistics about how the site is used: pages viewed, clicks on links,
      roughly where you are (country/city), and your device and browser. This does not tell us who you are.
    </p>

    <h2>Why we use it</h2>
    <p>
      To send you news about {s.artistName}: new music, videos, shows and merch, and, if you accept cookies, to
      understand how the site is used so we can improve it and our campaigns. The legal basis for both is your consent
      (GDPR article 6.1.a). We never sell your data.
    </p>

    <h2>Who handles it for us</h2>
    <p>
      Sign-ups are stored in Mailchimp (Intuit Inc.), which sends our emails and texts. Mailchimp may process data in the
      United States under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework and the EU standard contractual clauses. Statistics are
      handled by Google Analytics (Google Ireland Ltd), which may also transfer data to the United States under the same
      framework. Videos are played from YouTube (Google). The site is hosted by Netlify.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Sign-up details: until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete it. After that we remove it within 30 days. Statistics:
      Google Analytics keeps them for up to 14 months, and its cookies expire after at most 2 years.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask to see, correct, move or delete your data, and you can withdraw your consent at any time. Every email
      has an unsubscribe link, and you can reply STOP to any text. If you think we handle your data wrongly you can
      complain to the Swedish Authority for Privacy Protection (IMY), <a href="https://www.imy.se" target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">imy.se</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      We only set cookies if you accept them in the cookie banner. If you decline, nothing is loaded from Google
      Analytics. Your choice is remembered in your browser.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google Analytics sets a few cookies to tell visits apart and count page views. They expire after up to 2 years.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can change your mind at any time: <a href="#cookies" data-cookie-settings>cookie settings</a>. If you
      withdraw consent, the cookies are removed. The music videos are only loaded from YouTube (in its privacy-enhanced
      mode) when you press play; from then on YouTube’s own cookie and privacy policies apply. Links to streaming
      services, shops and social media take you to other sites, which have their own policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions or requests:{' '}
      {contactEmail ? <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> : <mark>[contact email]</mark>}
    </p>
  </main>

  <footer class="bottom">
    <Credits />
  </footer>
</Base>

<style>
  :global(html) {
    background: #000;
  }
  .top,
  .bottom {
    padding: var(--gutter);
  }
  .top a {
    color: #fff;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--caps-tracking);
  }
  .bottom {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: flex-end;
  }
  .policy {
    max-width: 640px;
    padding: clamp(24px, 6vw, 80px) var(--gutter) clamp(48px, 8vw, 120px);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-family: 'WT Kormelink', var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    line-height: 0.95;
  }
  .updated {
    margin: 0 0 40px;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 32px 0 8px;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--caps-tracking);
    word-spacing: var(--caps-word-spacing);
  }
  p,
  ul {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.1em;
  }
  a {
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  mark {
    background: #fff;
    color: #000;
  }
</style>
